---@field labels? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringMap Optional. User defined labels for the asset.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the asset was last updated.
---@field displayName? string Optional. User friendly display name.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the asset.
---@field resourceStatus? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetResourceStatus Output only. Status of the resource referenced by this asset.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the asset was created.

---Settings to manage the metadata discovery and publishing for an asset.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetDiscoverySpec
---@field schedule? string Optional. Cron schedule (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cron) for running discovery periodically. Successive discovery runs must be scheduled at least 60 minutes apart. The default value is to run discovery every 60 minutes.To explicitly set a timezone to the cron tab, apply a prefix in the cron tab: "CRON_TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}" or TZ=${IANA_TIME_ZONE}". The ${IANA_TIME_ZONE} may only be a valid string from IANA time zone database. For example, CRON_TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *, or TZ=America/New_York 1 * * * *.
---@field excludePatterns? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The list of patterns to apply for selecting data to exclude during discovery. For Cloud Storage bucket assets, these are interpreted as glob patterns used to match object names. For BigQuery dataset assets, these are interpreted as patterns to match table names.
---@field jsonOptions? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetDiscoverySpecJsonOptions Optional. Configuration for Json data.
---@field enabled? boolean Optional. Whether discovery is enabled.
---@field includePatterns? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The list of patterns to apply for selecting data to include during discovery if only a subset of the data should considered. For Cloud Storage bucket assets, these are interpreted as glob patterns used to match object names. For BigQuery dataset assets, these are interpreted as patterns to match table names.
---@field csvOptions? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetDiscoverySpecCsvOptions Optional. Configuration for CSV data.

---Describe CSV and similar semi-structured data formats.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetDiscoverySpecCsvOptions
---@field disableTypeInference? boolean Optional. Whether to disable the inference of data type for CSV data. If true, all columns will be registered as strings.
---@field encoding? string Optional. The character encoding of the data. The default is UTF-8.
---@field headerRows? number Optional. The number of rows to interpret as header rows that should be skipped when reading data rows.
---@field delimiter? string Optional. The delimiter being used to separate values. This defaults to ','.

---Describe JSON data format.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetDiscoverySpecJsonOptions
---@field disableTypeInference? boolean Optional. Whether to disable the inference of data type for Json data. If true, all columns will be registered as their primitive types (strings, number or boolean).
---@field encoding? string Optional. The character encoding of the data. The default is UTF-8.

