---Request message for CreateEntryLink.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1CreateEntryLinkRequest
---@field entryLinkId? string Required. Entry Link identifier * Must contain only lowercase letters, numbers and hyphens. * Must start with a letter. * Must be between 1-63 characters. * Must end with a number or a letter. * Must be unique within the EntryGroup.
---@field entryLink? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1EntryLink Required. Entry Link resource.
---@field parent? string Required. The resource name of the parent Entry Group: projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location_id}/entryGroups/{entry_group_id}.

---Create Entry request.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1CreateEntryRequest
---@field entry? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1Entry Required. Entry resource.
---@field parent? string Required. The resource name of the parent Entry Group: projects/{project}/locations/{location}/entryGroups/{entry_group}.
---@field entryId? string Required. Entry identifier. It has to be unique within an Entry Group.Entries corresponding to Google Cloud resources use an Entry ID format based on full resource names (https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/resource_names#full_resource_name). The format is a full resource name of the resource without the prefix double slashes in the API service name part of the full resource name. This allows retrieval of entries using their associated resource name.For example, if the full resource name of a resource is //library.googleapis.com/shelves/shelf1/books/book2, then the suggested entry_id is library.googleapis.com/shelves/shelf1/books/book2.It is also suggested to follow the same convention for entries corresponding to resources from providers or systems other than Google Cloud.The maximum size of the field is 4000 characters.

