---A data product is a curated collection of data assets, packaged to address specific use cases. It's a way to manage and share data in a more organized, product-like manner.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProduct
---@field icon? string Optional. Base64 encoded image representing the data product. Max Size: 3.0MiB Expected image dimensions are 512x512 pixels, however the API only performs validation on size of the encoded data. Note: For byte fields, the content of the fields are base64-encoded (which increases the size of the data by 33-36%) when using JSON on the wire.
---@field name? string Identifier. Resource name of the data product. Format: projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location_id}/dataProducts/{data_product_id}.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time at which the data product was created.
---@field labels? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringMap Optional. User-defined labels for the data product.Example: { "environment": "production", "billing": "marketing-department" }
---@field assetCount? number Output only. Number of data assets associated with this data product.
---@field ownerEmails? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Required. Emails of the data product owners.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time at which the data product was last updated.
---@field accessApprovalConfig? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessApprovalConfig Optional. Configuration for access approval for the data product.
---@field uid? string Output only. System generated unique ID for the data product. This ID will be different if the data product is deleted and re-created with the same name.
---@field accessGroups? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroupMap Optional. Data product access groups by access group id as key. If data product is used only for packaging data assets, then access groups may be empty. However, if a data product is used for sharing data assets, then at least one access group must be specified.Example: { "analyst": { "id": "analyst", "displayName": "Analyst", "description": "Access group for analysts", "principal": { "googleGroup": "analysts@example.com" } } }
---@field displayName? string Required. User-friendly display name of the data product.
---@field etag? string Optional. This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of other fields, and may be sent on update and delete requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the data product.

---Configuration for access approval for the data product.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessApprovalConfig
---@field approverEmails? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. Specifies the email addresses of users who are potential approvers and are notified when an access request is made for the data product. The maximum number of emails allowed is 10.

---Custom user defined access groups at the data product level. These are used for granting different levels of access (IAM roles) on the individual data product's data assets.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroup
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the access group.
---@field displayName? string Required. User friendly display name of the access group. Eg. "Analyst", "Developer", etc.
---@field defaultIamRoleConfig? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroupDefaultIamRoleConfig Optional. Default IAM role configuration to be applied on the data assets associated with this data product, for this access group.
---@field principal? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductPrincipal Required. The principal entity associated with this access group.
---@field id? string Required. Unique identifier of the access group within the data product. User defined. Eg. "analyst", "developer", etc.

---Default IAM role configuration for an access group.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroupDefaultIamRoleConfig
---@field role? string Optional. The IAM role resource name to be applied as default. Example: "roles/bigquery.dataViewer".

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroupMap { [string]: gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProductAccessGroup }

