---Contains name, type, mode and field type specific profile information.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfile
---@field fields? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldList Output only. List of fields with structural and profile information for each field.

---A field within a table.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileField
---@field mode? string Output only. The mode of the field. Possible values include: REQUIRED, if it is a required field. NULLABLE, if it is an optional field. REPEATED, if it is a repeated field.
---@field type? string Output only. The data type retrieved from the schema of the data source. For instance, for a BigQuery native table, it is the BigQuery Table Schema (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/rest/v2/tables#tablefieldschema). For a Dataplex Universal Catalog Entity, it is the Entity Schema (https://cloud.google.com/dataplex/docs/reference/rpc/google.cloud.dataplex.v1#type_3).
---@field name? string Output only. The name of the field.
---@field profile? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfo Output only. Profile information for the corresponding field.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileField[]

---The profile information for each field type.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfo
---@field distinctRatio? number Output only. Ratio of rows with distinct values against total scanned rows. Not available for complex non-groupable field type, including RECORD, ARRAY, GEOGRAPHY, and JSON, as well as fields with REPEATABLE mode.
---@field integerProfile? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoIntegerFieldInfo Integer type field information.
---@field doubleProfile? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoDoubleFieldInfo Double type field information.
---@field nullRatio? number Output only. Ratio of rows with null value against total scanned rows.
---@field topNValues? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoTopNValueList Output only. The list of top N non-null values, frequency and ratio with which they occur in the scanned data. N is 10 or equal to the number of distinct values in the field, whichever is smaller. Not available for complex non-groupable field type, including RECORD, ARRAY, GEOGRAPHY, and JSON, as well as fields with REPEATABLE mode.
---@field stringProfile? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoStringFieldInfo String type field information.

---The profile information for a double type field.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoDoubleFieldInfo
---@field average? number Output only. Average of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field min? number Output only. Minimum of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field max? number Output only. Maximum of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field standardDeviation? number Output only. Standard deviation of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field quartiles? gcp.dataplex_v1.DoubleList Output only. A quartile divides the number of data points into four parts, or quarters, of more-or-less equal size. Three main quartiles used are: The first quartile (Q1) splits off the lowest 25% of data from the highest 75%. It is also known as the lower or 25th empirical quartile, as 25% of the data is below this point. The second quartile (Q2) is the median of a data set. So, 50% of the data lies below this point. The third quartile (Q3) splits off the highest 25% of data from the lowest 75%. It is known as the upper or 75th empirical quartile, as 75% of the data lies below this point. Here, the quartiles is provided as an ordered list of quartile values for the scanned data, occurring in order Q1, median, Q3.

---The profile information for an integer type field.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoIntegerFieldInfo
---@field average? number Output only. Average of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field quartiles? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Output only. A quartile divides the number of data points into four parts, or quarters, of more-or-less equal size. Three main quartiles used are: The first quartile (Q1) splits off the lowest 25% of data from the highest 75%. It is also known as the lower or 25th empirical quartile, as 25% of the data is below this point. The second quartile (Q2) is the median of a data set. So, 50% of the data lies below this point. The third quartile (Q3) splits off the highest 25% of data from the lowest 75%. It is known as the upper or 75th empirical quartile, as 75% of the data lies below this point. Here, the quartiles is provided as an ordered list of approximate quartile values for the scanned data, occurring in order Q1, median, Q3.
---@field min? string Output only. Minimum of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field max? string Output only. Maximum of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.
---@field standardDeviation? number Output only. Standard deviation of non-null values in the scanned data. NaN, if the field has a NaN.

---The profile information for a string type field.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoStringFieldInfo
---@field averageLength? number Output only. Average length of non-null values in the scanned data.
---@field maxLength? string Output only. Maximum length of non-null values in the scanned data.
---@field minLength? string Output only. Minimum length of non-null values in the scanned data.

---Top N non-null values in the scanned data.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoTopNValue
---@field value? string Output only. String value of a top N non-null value.
---@field ratio? number Output only. Ratio of the corresponding value in the field against the total number of rows in the scanned data.
---@field count? string Output only. Count of the corresponding value in the scanned data.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoTopNValueList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileResultProfileFieldProfileInfoTopNValue[]

---DataProfileScan related setting.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpec
---@field catalogPublishingEnabled? boolean Optional. If set, the latest DataScan job result will be published as Dataplex Universal Catalog metadata.
---@field rowFilter? string Optional. A filter applied to all rows in a single DataScan job. The filter needs to be a valid SQL expression for a WHERE clause in BigQuery standard SQL syntax. Example: col1 >= 0 AND col2 < 10
---@field includeFields? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecSelectedFields Optional. The fields to include in data profile.If not specified, all fields at the time of profile scan job execution are included, except for ones listed in exclude_fields.
---@field postScanActions? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecPostScanActions Optional. Actions to take upon job completion..
---@field excludeFields? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecSelectedFields Optional. The fields to exclude from data profile.If specified, the fields will be excluded from data profile, regardless of include_fields value.
---@field mode? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecModeEnum|string Optional. The execution mode for the profile scan.
---@field samplingPercent? number Optional. The percentage of the records to be selected from the dataset for DataScan. Value can range between 0.0 and 100.0 with up to 3 significant decimal digits. Sampling is not applied if sampling_percent is not specified, 0 or 100.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecModeEnum "MODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD"|"LIGHTWEIGHT"

---The configuration of post scan actions of DataProfileScan job.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecPostScanActions
---@field bigqueryExport? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecPostScanActionsBigQueryExport Optional. If set, results will be exported to the provided BigQuery table.

---The configuration of BigQuery export post scan action.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecPostScanActionsBigQueryExport
---@field resultsTable? string Optional. The BigQuery table to export DataProfileScan results to. Format: //bigquery.googleapis.com/projects/PROJECT_ID/datasets/DATASET_ID/tables/TABLE_ID

---The specification for fields to include or exclude in data profile scan.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataProfileSpecSelectedFields
---@field fieldNames? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. Expected input is a list of fully qualified names of fields as in the schema.Only top-level field names for nested fields are supported. For instance, if 'x' is of nested field type, listing 'x' is supported but 'x.y.z' is not supported. Here 'y' and 'y.z' are nested fields of 'x'.

---DataQualityColumnResult provides a more detailed, per-column view of the results.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityColumnResult
---@field score? number Output only. The column-level data quality score for this data scan job if and only if the 'column' field is set.The score ranges between between 0, 100 (up to two decimal points).
---@field column? string Output only. The column specified in the DataQualityRule.
---@field passed? boolean Output only. Whether the column passed or failed.
---@field dimensions? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimensionResultList Output only. The dimension-level results for this column.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityColumnResultList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityColumnResult[]

---A dimension captures data quality intent about a defined subset of the rules specified.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimension
---@field name? string Output only. The dimension name a rule belongs to. Custom dimension name is supported with all uppercase letters and maximum length of 30 characters.

---DataQualityDimensionResult provides a more detailed, per-dimension view of the results.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimensionResult
---@field passed? boolean Output only. Whether the dimension passed or failed.
---@field score? number Output only. The dimension-level data quality score for this data scan job if and only if the 'dimension' field is set.The score ranges between 0, 100 (up to two decimal points).
---@field dimension? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimension Output only. The dimension config specified in the DataQualitySpec, as is.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimensionResultList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimensionResult[]

---The output of a DataQualityScan.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResult
---@field passed? boolean Output only. Overall data quality result -- true if all rules passed.
---@field postScanActionsResult? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultPostScanActionsResult Output only. The result of post scan actions.
---@field anomalyDetectionGeneratedAssets? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultAnomalyDetectionGeneratedAssets Output only. The generated assets for anomaly detection.
---@field columns? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityColumnResultList Output only. A list of results at the column level.A column will have a corresponding DataQualityColumnResult if and only if there is at least one rule with the 'column' field set to it.
---@field catalogPublishingStatus? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataScanCatalogPublishingStatus Output only. The status of publishing the data scan as Dataplex Universal Catalog metadata.
---@field scannedData? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1ScannedData Output only. The data scanned for this result.
---@field rules? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleResultList Output only. A list of all the rules in a job, and their results.
---@field rowCount? string Output only. The count of rows processed.
---@field score? number Output only. The overall data quality score.The score ranges between 0, 100 (up to two decimal points).
---@field dimensions? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityDimensionResultList Output only. A list of results at the dimension level.A dimension will have a corresponding DataQualityDimensionResult if and only if there is at least one rule with the 'dimension' field set to it.

---The assets generated by Anomaly Detection Data Scan.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultAnomalyDetectionGeneratedAssets
---@field dataIntermediateTable? string Output only. The intermediate table for data anomaly detection. Format: PROJECT_ID.DATASET_ID.TABLE_ID
---@field resultTable? string Output only. The result table for anomaly detection. Format: PROJECT_ID.DATASET_ID.TABLE_ID If the result table is set at AnomalyDetectionAssets, the result table here would be the same as the one set in the AnomalyDetectionAssets.result_table.
---@field freshnessIntermediateTable? string Output only. The intermediate table for freshness anomaly detection. Format: PROJECT_ID.DATASET_ID.TABLE_ID
---@field volumeIntermediateTable? string Output only. The intermediate table for volume anomaly detection. Format: PROJECT_ID.DATASET_ID.TABLE_ID

