---The result of BigQuery export post scan action.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultPostScanActionsResultBigQueryExportResult
---@field state? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultPostScanActionsResultBigQueryExportResultStateEnum|string Output only. Execution state for the BigQuery exporting.
---@field message? string Output only. Additional information about the BigQuery exporting.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityResultPostScanActionsResultBigQueryExportResultStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SUCCEEDED"|"FAILED"|"SKIPPED"

---A rule captures data quality intent about a data source.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRule
---@field column? string Optional. The unnested column which this rule is evaluated against.
---@field nonNullExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleNonNullExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each column value is null.
---@field suspended? boolean Optional. Whether the Rule is active or suspended. Default is false.
---@field statisticRangeExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleStatisticRangeExpectation Aggregate rule which evaluates whether the column aggregate statistic lies between a specified range.
---@field debugQueries? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleDebugQueryList Optional. Specifies the debug queries for this rule. Currently, only one query is supported, but this may be expanded in the future.
---@field name? string Optional. A mutable name for the rule. The name must contain only letters (a-z, A-Z), numbers (0-9), or hyphens (-). The maximum length is 63 characters. Must start with a letter. Must end with a number or a letter.
---@field threshold? number Optional. The minimum ratio of passing_rows / total_rows required to pass this rule, with a range of 0.0, 1.0.0 indicates default value (i.e. 1.0).This field is only valid for row-level type rules.
---@field templateReference? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleTemplateReference Aggregate rule which references a rule template and provides the parameters to be substituted in the template. If any rows are returned, this rule fails.
---@field rangeExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRangeExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each column value lies between a specified range.
---@field ignoreNull? boolean Optional. Rows with null values will automatically fail a rule, unless ignore_null is true. In that case, such null rows are trivially considered passing.This field is only valid for the following type of rules: RangeExpectation RegexExpectation SetExpectation UniquenessExpectation
---@field regexExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRegexExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each column value matches a specified regex.
---@field dimension? string Optional. The dimension a rule belongs to. Results are also aggregated at the dimension level. Custom dimension name is supported with all uppercase letters and maximum length of 30 characters.
---@field tableConditionExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleTableConditionExpectation Aggregate rule which evaluates whether the provided expression is true for a table.
---@field attributes? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringMap Optional. Map of attribute name and value linked to the rule. The rules to evaluate can be filtered based on attributes provided here and a filter expression provided in the DataQualitySpec.filter field.
---@field rowConditionExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRowConditionExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each row in a table passes the specified condition.
---@field ruleSource? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRuleSource Output only. Contains information about the source of the rule and its relationship with the BigQuery table, where applicable.
---@field sqlAssertion? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleSqlAssertion Aggregate rule which evaluates the number of rows returned for the provided statement. If any rows are returned, this rule fails.
---@field uniquenessExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleUniquenessExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each column value is unique.
---@field setExpectation? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleSetExpectation Row-level rule which evaluates whether each column value is contained by a specified set.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the rule. The maximum length is 1,024 characters.

---Specifies a SQL statement that is evaluated to return up to 10 scalar values that are used to debug rules. If the rule fails, the values can help diagnose the cause of the failure.The SQL statement must use GoogleSQL syntax (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/query-syntax), and must not contain any semicolons.You can use the data reference parameter ${data()} to reference the source table with all of its precondition filters applied. Examples of precondition filters include row filters, incremental data filters, and sampling. For more information, see Data reference parameter (https://cloud.google.com/dataplex/docs/auto-data-quality-overview#data-reference-parameter).You can also name results with an explicit alias using [AS] alias. For more information, see BigQuery explicit aliases (https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/query-syntax#explicit_alias_syntax).Example: SELECT MIN(col1) AS min_col1, MAX(col1) AS max_col1 FROM ${data()}
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleDebugQuery
---@field sqlStatement? string Required. Specifies the SQL statement to be executed.
---@field description? string Optional. Specifies the description of the debug query. The maximum length is 1,024 characters.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleDebugQueryList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleDebugQuery[]

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRule[]

---Evaluates whether each column value is null.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleNonNullExpectation

---Evaluates whether each column value lies between a specified range.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRangeExpectation
---@field minValue? string Optional. The minimum column value allowed for a row to pass this validation. At least one of min_value and max_value need to be provided.
---@field strictMaxEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether each value needs to be strictly lesser than ('<') the maximum, or if equality is allowed.Only relevant if a max_value has been defined. Default = false.
---@field strictMinEnabled? boolean Optional. Whether each value needs to be strictly greater than ('>') the minimum, or if equality is allowed.Only relevant if a min_value has been defined. Default = false.
---@field maxValue? string Optional. The maximum column value allowed for a row to pass this validation. At least one of min_value and max_value need to be provided.

---Evaluates whether each column value matches a specified regex.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleRegexExpectation
---@field regex? string Optional. A regular expression the column value is expected to match.

---DataQualityRuleResult provides a more detailed, per-rule view of the results.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleResult
---@field rule? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRule Output only. The rule specified in the DataQualitySpec, as is.
---@field failingRowsQuery? string Output only. The query to find rows that did not pass this rule.This field is only valid for row-level type rules.
---@field assertionRowCount? string Output only. The number of rows returned by the SQL statement in a SQL assertion rule.This field is only valid for SQL assertion rules.
---@field debugQueriesResultSets? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1DataQualityRuleResultDebugQueryResultSetList Output only. Contains the results of all debug queries for this rule. The number of result sets will correspond to the number of debug_queries.
---@field passed? boolean Output only. Whether the rule passed or failed.
---@field evaluatedCount? string Output only. The number of rows a rule was evaluated against.This field is only valid for row-level type rules.Evaluated count can be configured to either include all rows (default) - with null rows automatically failing rule evaluation, or exclude null rows from the evaluated_count, by setting ignore_nulls = true.This field is not set for rule SqlAssertion.
---@field nullCount? string Output only. The number of rows with null values in the specified column.
---@field passedCount? string Output only. The number of rows which passed a rule evaluation.This field is only valid for row-level type rules.This field is not set for rule SqlAssertion.
---@field passRatio? number Output only. The ratio of passed_count / evaluated_count.This field is only valid for row-level type rules.

---Contains a single result from the debug query.
