---A lake is a centralized repository for managing enterprise data across the organization distributed across many cloud projects, and stored in a variety of storage services such as Google Cloud Storage and BigQuery. The resources attached to a lake are referred to as managed resources. Data within these managed resources can be structured or unstructured. A lake provides data admins with tools to organize, secure and manage their data at scale, and provides data scientists and data engineers an integrated experience to easily search, discover, analyze and transform data and associated metadata.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1Lake
---@field metastore? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1LakeMetastore Optional. Settings to manage lake and Dataproc Metastore service instance association.
---@field serviceAccount? string Output only. Service account associated with this lake. This service account must be authorized to access or operate on resources managed by the lake.
---@field metastoreStatus? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1LakeMetastoreStatus Output only. Metastore status of the lake.
---@field assetStatus? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1AssetStatus Output only. Aggregated status of the underlying assets of the lake.
---@field labels? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringMap Optional. User-defined labels for the lake.
---@field name? string Output only. The relative resource name of the lake, of the form: projects/{project_number}/locations/{location_id}/lakes/{lake_id}.
---@field displayName? string Optional. User friendly display name.
---@field state? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1LakeStateEnum Output only. Current state of the lake.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the lake was last updated.
---@field uid? string Output only. System generated globally unique ID for the lake. This ID will be different if the lake is deleted and re-created with the same name.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the lake was created.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the lake.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1LakeList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1Lake[]

