---MetadataFeed contains information related to the metadata feed.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeed
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the metadata feed, in the format projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location_id}/metadataFeeds/{metadata_feed_id}.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time when the feed was created.
---@field labels? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringMap Optional. User-defined labels.
---@field filters? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFilters Optional. The filters of the metadata feed. Only the changes that match the filters are published.
---@field pubsubTopic? string Optional. The pubsub topic that you want the metadata feed messages to publish to. Please grant Dataplex service account the permission to publish messages to the topic. The service account is: service-{PROJECT_NUMBER}@gcp-sa-dataplex.iam.gserviceaccount.com.
---@field scope? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedScope Required. The scope of the metadata feed. Only the in scope changes are published.
---@field uid? string Output only. A system-generated, globally unique ID for the metadata job. If the metadata job is deleted and then re-created with the same name, this ID is different.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The time when the feed was updated.

---Filters defines the type of changes that you want to listen to. You can have multiple entry type filters and multiple aspect type filters. All of the entry type filters are OR'ed together. All of the aspect type filters are OR'ed together. All of the entry type filters and aspect type filters are AND'ed together.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFilters
---@field aspectTypes? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The aspect types that you want to listen to. Depending on how the aspect is attached to the entry, in the format: projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location}/aspectTypes/{aspect_type_id}.
---@field changeTypes? gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFiltersChangeTypesItemEnumList Optional. The type of change that you want to listen to. If not specified, all changes are published.
---@field entryTypes? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The entry types that you want to listen to, specified as relative resource names in the format projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location}/entryTypes/{entry_type_id}. Only entries that belong to the specified entry types are published.

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFiltersChangeTypesItemEnum "CHANGE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"CREATE"|"UPDATE"|"DELETE"

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFiltersChangeTypesItemEnumList (gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedFiltersChangeTypesItemEnum|string)[]

---@alias gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedList gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeed[]

---Scope defines the scope of the metadata feed. Scopes are exclusive. Only one of the scopes can be specified.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleCloudDataplexV1MetadataFeedScope
---@field entryGroups? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The entry groups whose entries you want to listen to. Must be in the format: projects/{project_id_or_number}/locations/{location_id}/entryGroups/{entry_group_id}.
---@field organizationLevel? boolean Optional. Whether the metadata feed is at the organization-level. If true, all changes happened to the entries in the same organization as the feed are published. If false, you must specify a list of projects or a list of entry groups whose entries you want to listen to.The default is false.
---@field projects? gcp.dataplex_v1.StringList Optional. The projects whose entries you want to listen to. Must be in the same organization as the feed. Must be in the format: projects/{project_id_or_number}.

