---This resource represents a long-running operation that is the result of a network API call.
---@class gcp.dataplex_v1.GoogleLongrunningOperation
---@field metadata? gcp.dataplex_v1.DocumentMap Service-specific metadata associated with the operation. It typically contains progress information and common metadata such as create time. Some services might not provide such metadata. Any method that returns a long-running operation should document the metadata type, if any.
---@field response? gcp.dataplex_v1.DocumentMap The normal, successful response of the operation. If the original method returns no data on success, such as Delete, the response is google.protobuf.Empty. If the original method is standard Get/Create/Update, the response should be the resource. For other methods, the response should have the type XxxResponse, where Xxx is the original method name. For example, if the original method name is TakeSnapshot(), the inferred response type is TakeSnapshotResponse.
